Test stack overflow, underflow, scribbling handing through a user process.

This test compiles a kernel module that will perform a proces underflow,
overflow and scribbling, depending on the parameter passed on insertion.

Test inputs:
    script -O output.log -c \"./stackman $mode\"  <=== where mode will be overflow, underflow, and scribbling
    rlAssertGrep "Segmentation fault" "output.log"
    rlAssertGrep "COMMAND_EXIT_CODE=\"139\"" "output.log"

Expected result:
  All tests should cause a segmentation fault as the kernel protects itself and provides the following results.
  For overflow:
    [   PASS   ] :: Run overflow program (SEGFAULT expected) (Expected 0, got 0)
    [   PASS   ] :: File 'output.log' should contain 'Segmentation fault'
    [   PASS   ] :: File 'output.log' should contain 'COMMAND_EXIT_CODE="139"'
  For underflow:
    [   PASS   ] :: Run underflow program (SEGFAULT expected) (Expected 0, got 0)
    [   PASS   ] :: File 'output.log' should contain 'Segmentation fault'
    [   PASS   ] :: File 'output.log' should contain 'COMMAND_EXIT_CODE="139"'
  For scribbling:
    [   PASS   ] :: Run scribbling program (SEGFAULT expected) (Expected 0, got 0)
    [   PASS   ] :: File 'output.log' should contain 'Segmentation fault'
    [   PASS   ] :: File 'output.log' should contain 'COMMAND_EXIT_CODE="139"'

Results location:
    output.txt
